cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "GravOp: fast gravothermal evolution of self-interacting dark matter haloes, with a kinetically tested conductivity closure"
abstract: "Source release of a semi-implicit Lagrangian gravothermal solver for self-interacting dark matter haloes, its selectable conductivity closure, a Fourier neural operator emulator with a learned collapse clock and clock-error-aware uncertainty, static baryonic potentials and a Bayesian inference pipeline. It includes the code of the closure test against NSphere particle simulations (particle-number ladders, four pre-registered haloes, the five- and seven-halo fits), the figure scripts, the acceptance suite, and the statecond benchmark of conditioning coordinates for neural PDE surrogates. The machine-readable results, per-run particle measurements and rendered figures are deposited in a companion archival record."
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-12"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/salahgo/gravop"
url: "https://github.com/salahgo/gravop"
authors:
